tiltalign Version 5.2.17 Sep 19 2026 00:48:39
Copyright (C) 1994-2025 by the Regents of the University of Colorado
Usage: tiltalign [Options] input_file output_file
Options can be abbreviated, current short name abbreviations are in parentheses
Options:

INPUT AND OUTPUT FILE OPTIONS
 -ModelFile   File
    Input fiducial model file
 -ImageFile   File
    Image file that fiducial model was built on (optional)
 -ImageSizeXandY   2 ints
    Dimensions of image file (optional)
 -ImageOriginXandY   2 floats
    X and Y origin values from image file header (optional)
 -ImagePixelSizeXandY   2 floats
    X and Y Pixel spacing from image file header, in Angstroms (optional)
 -UnbinnedPixelSize   Float
    Pixel size of unbinned data in nanometers
 -ImagesAreBinned   Int
    The binning of the images relative to the original data (default 1)
 -OutputModelFile   File
    Output file for 3-D model of solved fiducial positions
 -OutputResidualFile   File
    Output file for list of all residuals
 -OutputModelAndResidual   File
    Root name for output of both a 3-D model and residuals
 -OutputFilledInModel   File
    Output file for fiducial model with missing points filled in
 -OutputTopBotResiduals   File
    Root name for separate output of residuals for top and bottom points
 -OutputFidXYZFile   File
    File for text output of the solved X-Y-Z coordinates
 -FixedXYZInputFile   File
    File with fixed X-Y-Z coordinates to use in local alignments
 -OutputTiltFile   File
    Output file for the solved tilt angles after adjustment for beam tilt
 -OutputUnadjustedTiltFile   File
    Output file for the solved tilt angles before adjustment for beam tilt
 -OutputXAxisTiltFile   File
    Output file for tilts around the X axis.
 -OutputTransformFile   File
    Output file for 2-D transformations needed to align images
 -OutputZFactorFile   File
    Output file for factors to adjust X and Y as function of Z in
    backprojection

ANGLE AND VIEW RELATED OPTIONS
 -IncludeStartEndInc   3 ints
    Starting and ending view numbers, and increment between views, to include
    in analysis
 -IncludeList   List
    List of views to include in the analysis
 -ExcludeList   List
    List of views to exclude from the analysis
 -RotationAngle   Float
    Initial rotation angle from the Y axis to the tilt axis
 -SeparateGroup   List
    List of views that should be grouped separately in automapping
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -NoSeparateTiltGroups   Int
    Group tilt angles across separate groups (1 for patch track, 2 for any)
 -first (-f)  OR  -FirstTiltAngle   Float
    Tilt angle of first view in degrees
 -increment (-i)  OR  -TiltIncrement   Float
    Increment between tilt angles
 -tiltfile (-t)  OR  -TiltFile   File
    File with tilt angles
 -angles (-a)  OR  -TiltAngles   Floats
    Individual tilt angles for each view
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -AngleOffset   Float
    Amount to add to all entered tilt angles

GLOBAL VARIABLE SELECTION OPTIONS
 -ProjectionStretch
    Solve for axis skew applying to projection of all images.
 -BeamTiltOption   Int
    Type of beam tilt solution: 0 for none, 1 to include in fit, 2 to search
 -FixedOrInitialBeamTilt   Float
    Initial value of beam tilt when solving for it, or fixed value when not
 -RotOption   Int
    Type of rotation solution: 0 for none, 1 for independent, 2 for mapped, 3
    or 4 for automapped, -1 for single variable
 -RotDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping rotation variables
 -RotNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of
    rotation variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -RotationFixedView   Int
    View to fix at the initial rotation angle
 -TiltOption   Int
    Type of tilt angle solution: 0 for all fixed, 2 for all independent, 5 for
    automapping
 -TiltFixedView   Int
    View at which to fix the tilt angle (TiltOption 1, 3, 7, or 8)
 -TiltSecondFixedView   Int
    Second view at which to fix the tilt angle (TiltOption 7 or 8)
 -TiltDefaultGrouping   Int
    Average default group size when automapping tilt variables
 -TiltNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of tilt
    variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -MagReferenceView   Int
    Reference view whose magnification will be fixed at 1.0
 -MagOption   Int
    Type of magnification solution: 0 fixed, 1 independent, 2 mapped, 3 or 4
    automapped.
 -MagDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping magnification variables
 -MagNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of
    magnification variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -CompReferenceView   Int
    View to fix at compression 1.0
 -CompOption   Int
    Type of compression solution: 0 fixed, 1 independent, 2 mapped, 3 or 4
    automapped
 -CompDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping compression variables
 -CompNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of
    compression variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -XStretchOption   Int
    Type of X-stretch solution: 0 fixed, 1 independent, 2 mapped, 3 or 4
    automapped
 -XStretchDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default average group size when automapping X stretch variables
 -XStretchNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of X
    stretch variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -SkewOption   Int
    Type of skew solution: 0 fixed, 1 independent, 2 mapped, 3 or 4 automapped
 -SkewDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping skew variables
 -SkewNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of skew
    variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -XTiltOption   Int
    Type of X-axis tilt solution: 0 fixed, 1 independent, 2 mapped, 3 or 4
    automapped
 -XTiltDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping X-axis tilt variables
 -XTiltNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of X-axis
    tilt variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)

MINIMIZATION AND OUTPUT OPTIONS
 -ResidualReportCriterion   Float
    Criterion number of SDs above mean residual error to report (negative for
    SDs relative to neighbors)
 -SurfacesToAnalyze   Int
    1 or 2 to determine surface angles by fitting points to 1 or 2 surfaces,
    or 0 for no fit
 -MetroFactor   Float
    Step size for minimization procedure
 -MaximumCycles   Int
    Limit on number of cycles for minimization procedure (default 1000)
 -AxisZShift   Float
    Amount to shift tilt axis in Z, or 1000 to put at midpoint of range
 -ShiftZFromOriginal
    Apply Z shift relative to original tilt axis location
 -AxisXShift   Float
    Amount to shift the tilt axis in X

ROBUST FITTING, WEIGHTING, AND CROSS-VALIDATION OPTIONS
 -RobustFitting
    Do robust fitting by giving less or no weight to outliers
 -WeightWholeTracks
    Do robust fitting by weighting entire contours in patch track models
 -KFactorScaling   Float
    Amount to scale the K factor that controls how many points are
    down-weighted
 -WarnOnRobustFailure
    Do not give error if robust fitting fails and alignment is just global
 -MinWeightGroupSizes   2 ints
    Minimum sizes of groups of points for computing weights, global and local
 -ObjectsWithExtraWeight   List
    List of model objects to be given special weighting
 -ExtraWeights   Floats
    Special weighting factors for objects (just one, or one per object)
 -CrossValidate   Int
    1 to leave out sets of points in multiple runs, 2 for local runs only
 -FractionToLeaveOut   2 floats
    Fraction of points to leave out of each cross-validation run
 -LeaveOutPredictAndPad   2 ints
    # of contiguous views to predict and padding views to leave out
 -CVCoverageTargetOrFactor
    Target number of points, or multiple of total points, to leave out
 -CVMinAndMaxCoverageFactor
    Minimum and maximum values for coverage factor
 -RandomSeed   Int
    Specific seed value for cross-validation, or 0 for time-based value
 -TestSetIntervalOrFrac   Float
    Interval between points or fraction of points to use for test set

LOCAL ALIGNMENT OPTIONS
 -LocalAlignments
    Do alignments with subsets of points in local areas
 -OutputLocalFile   File
    Output file for transformations for local alignments
 -TargetPatchSizeXandY   2 ints
    Target minimum size for local patches in X and Y
 -NumberOfLocalPatchesXandY   2 ints
    Number of local patches in X and Y over full area for local solutions
 -MinSizeOrOverlapXandY   2 floats
    Minimum fractional overlap in X and Y (if < 1) or minimum size of patches
    (if > 1).
 -MinFidsTotalAndEachSurface   2 ints
    Minimum total number of fiducials, and minimum number present on each
    surface if two surfaces exist
 -FixXYZCoordinates
    Fix the X-Y-Z coordinates of the fiducials at their global values
 -LocalOutputOptions   3 ints
    1 for parameter output, 1 for X-Y-Z coordinate output, and 1 for high
    residual output

LOCAL VARIABLE SELECTION OPTIONS
 -LocalRotOption   Int
    Type of local rotation solution: 0 for none, 1 for independent, 2 for
    mapped, 3 or 4 for automapped, -1 for single variable
 -LocalRotDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping local rotation variables
 -LocalRotNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of local
    rotation variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalTiltOption   Int
    Type of local tilt angle solution; same values as for global
 -LocalTiltFixedView   Int
    View at which to fix the tilt angle (LocalTiltOption 1, 3, 7, or 8)
 -LocalTiltSecondFixedView   Int
    Second view at which to fix the tilt angle (LocalTiltOption 7 or 8)
 -LocalTiltDefaultGrouping   Int
    Average default group size when automapping local tilt variables
 -LocalTiltNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of local
    tilt variables
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalMagReferenceView   Int
    Reference view whose local magnification will be fixed at 1.0
 -LocalMagOption   Int
    Type of local magnification solution; same values as for global
 -LocalMagDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping local magnification variables
 -LocalMagNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of local
    magnification variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalXStretchOption   Int
    Type of local X-stretch solution; same values as for global
 -LocalXStretchDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default average group size when automapping local X stretch variables
 -LocalXStretchNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of local
    X stretch variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalSkewOption   Int
    Type of local skew solution; same values as for global
 -LocalSkewDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping local skew variables
 -LocalSkewNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of local
    skew variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalXTiltOption   Int
    Type of local X-axis tilt solution; same values as for global
 -LocalXTiltDefaultGrouping   Int
    Default group size when automapping local X-axis tilt variables
 -LocalXTiltNondefaultGroup   3 ints
    Starting and ending views and group size for nondefault grouping of local
    X-axis tilt variables.
    (Successive entries accumulate)

MAPPING OPTIONS
 -RotMapping   Ints
    Rotation variable number for each view (if RotOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalRotMapping   Ints
    Local rotation variable number for each view (if LocalRotOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -TiltMapping   Ints
    Tilt variable number for each view (if TiltOption 4)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalTiltMapping   Ints
    Local tilt variable number for each view (if LocalTiltOption 4)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -MagMapping   Ints
    Magnification variable number for each view (if MagOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalMagMapping   Ints
    Local magnification variable number for each view (if LocalMagOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -CompMapping   Ints
    Compression variable number for each view (if CompOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -XStretchMapping   Ints
    X stretch variable number for each view (if XStretchOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalXStretchMapping   Ints
    Local X stretch variable number for each view (if LocalXStretchOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -SkewMapping   Ints
    Skew variable number for each view (if SkewOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalSkewMapping   Ints
    Local skew variable number for each view (if LocalSkewOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -XTiltMapping   Ints
    X-axis tilt variable number for each view (if XTiltOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)
 -LocalXTiltMapping   Ints
    Local X-axis tilt variable number for each view (if LocalXTiltOption 2)
    (Successive entries accumulate)

OTHER OPTIONS
 -CreatedDayStamp   Int
    A value for when the command file was created (days since 1/1/20).
 -param (-p)  OR  -ParameterFile   File
    Read parameter entries from file
 -help (-h)  OR  -usage
    Print help output
